## Proposal

### What is the root cause of that problem?

In the OP's video the tracked expense is created in the **Self DM**, so when the whisper flow starts the report under the money‑request RHP is the Self DM. Selecting a workspace routes the flow to the confirmation step keyed to the **destination** report (the policy expense chat), e.g. [`ReportUtils.ts#L12001`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/3f4e1a173b6b0e8b538c077cfef1d7af082e3659/src/libs/ReportUtils.ts#L12001). Because navigating to that RHP route also aligns the full‑screen route under the overlay ([`linkTo/index.ts#L222-L238`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/3f4e1a173b6b0e8b538c077cfef1d7af082e3659/src/libs/Navigation/helpers/linkTo/index.ts#L222-L238)), the Reports split's central report is **swapped from the Self DM to the destination workspace chat** — verifiable in the confirmation step, where the `user's expenses` header already renders under the confirmation dialog.

On confirm, `navigateAfterExpenseCreate` takes the non‑global‑create branch and calls `dismissModalAndOpenReportInInboxTab(destinationReportID)` ([`navigateAfterExpenseCreate.ts#L57-L60`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/3f4e1a173b6b0e8b538c077cfef1d7af082e3659/src/libs/Navigation/helpers/navigateAfterExpenseCreate.ts#L57-L60)) → `dismissModalWithReport({reportID})` ([`dismissModalAndOpenReportInInboxTab.ts#L84`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/3f4e1a173b6b0e8b538c077cfef1d7af082e3659/src/libs/Navigation/helpers/dismissModalAndOpenReportInInboxTab.ts#L84)). Since the topmost report is now the destination (`topmostReportID === reportID`) and the Reports split is topmost, this hits the early branch that **only dismisses the modal, without re‑navigating** ([`Navigation.ts#L919-L925`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/3f4e1a173b6b0e8b538c077cfef1d7af082e3659/src/libs/Navigation/Navigation.ts#L919-L925)). The RHP peels off to reveal `[Sidebar, workspaceChat]` — the Self DM is no longer in the stack — so tapping back lands on the Inbox instead of the Self Chat.

### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?

**Open the destination workspace chat with `backTo` set to the originating Self DM**, so its header back button returns there regardless of what the swap left in the stack — report headers already resolve back via `goBack(backTo)`, so this is the deterministic mechanism the flow is missing.

**Thread the source report through the terminal navigation.** The move‑from‑track flow already knows the origin as the draft's `linkedTrackedExpenseReportID`. Pass it as `backTo` from `navigateAfterExpenseCreate`'s dismiss branch into `dismissModalAndOpenReportInInboxTab` → `dismissModalWithReport`, building it once with `ROUTES.REPORT_WITH_ID.getRoute(linkedTrackedExpenseReportID)`.

**Honor it in the collapsed branch.** In `dismissModalWithReport` at [`Navigation.ts#L919-L925`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/3f4e1a173b6b0e8b538c077cfef1d7af082e3659/src/libs/Navigation/Navigation.ts#L919-L925), when the topmost report already equals `reportID` **and** a `backTo` was supplied, re‑open it with the param instead of a bare dismiss:

```ts
if (topmostReportID === reportID && areReportsIDsDefined && isReportsSplitTopmostFullScreen) {
    options?.onBeforeNavigate?.(false);
    dismissModal({
        afterTransition: backTo ? () => navigate(ROUTES.REPORT_WITH_ID.getRoute(reportID, reportActionID, referrer, backTo), {forceReplace: true}) : options?.afterTransition,
    });
    return;
}
```

This is scoped to the move‑from‑track paths (`CATEGORIZE`/`SHARE`/`SUBMIT`), since only they launch from a report the user expects to return to; the global‑create case passes no `backTo` and keeps today's "open on the inbox tab" behavior, so no other consumer of `dismissModalAndOpenReportInInboxTab` changes.

### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)

- **Keep the Self DM under the overlay** (suppress the full‑screen swap in `linkTo` for these RHP steps) so the terminal `dismissModalWithReport` pushes the destination on top of the Self DM. Fixes back navigation but touches the shared overlay logic in `linkTo`, which many RHP flows rely on — higher blast radius than attaching a `backTo`.
- **Land back on the Self DM and push the workspace chat on top.** Rejected: the video's expected result is to land on the workspace chat first and only return to Self Chat on back, so the destination must remain the visible screen.

## Proposal

### Please re-state the problem that we are trying to solve in this issue.

On narrow layout (iOS app), after submitting a tracked expense from the self-DM to a workspace via the "Submit it to someone" whisper, the app opens the workspace chat — but pressing the back button lands on the Inbox instead of returning to the self-DM the user came from.

### What is the root cause of that problem?

While the expense confirmation RHP is open on narrow layout, the destination workspace chat is pre-mounted underneath the RHP so it can be revealed instantly on dismiss: [`getSubmitExpensePreMountDestinationRoute`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/pages/iou/request/step/confirmation/getSubmitExpensePreMountDestinationRoute.ts#L44-L92) returns `REPORT_WITH_ID(workspaceChat)`, and [`usePreMountDestination` dispatches it via `Navigation.preInsertFullscreenUnderRHP`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/hooks/usePreMountDestination/index.ts#L63), which fires a `REPLACE_FULLSCREEN_UNDER_RHP` action.

Because every report route resolves to the `TAB_NAVIGATOR` fullscreen, [`handleReplaceFullscreenUnderRHP` takes the tab branch](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/AppNavigator/createRootStackNavigator/GetStateForActionHandlers.ts#L432-L463) and rebuilds the Reports split navigator through `getTargetTabRoute`. That's where the history is lost: [it keeps only the FIRST existing nested route (`existingFirstRoute` — the Inbox sidebar) as the back target and throws away every route above it](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/AppNavigator/createRootStackNavigator/GetStateForActionHandlers.ts#L232-L237) — including the self-DM report the flow started from:

```
before pre-insert:  REPORTS_SPLIT: [Inbox, Report(selfDM)]        <- RHP on top
after pre-insert:   REPORTS_SPLIT: [Inbox, Report(workspaceChat)] <- selfDM dropped
```

So when the RHP dismisses and the user presses back on the workspace chat, the stack pops to the Inbox sidebar.

I verified this against the real handler with a unit test (same harness as the existing `handleReplaceFullscreenUnderRHP.test.ts`): given `[Inbox, Report(100)]` under the RHP and a pre-insert of `Report(200)`, the handler returns `[Inbox, Report(200)]` — `Report(100)` is gone.

### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?

In [`getTargetTabRoute`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/AppNavigator/createRootStackNavigator/GetStateForActionHandlers.ts#L207-L237), preserve the tab's entire existing nested stack beneath the incoming screen instead of only its first route. The `WORKSPACE_NAVIGATOR` branch (which deliberately seeds a fresh `WORKSPACES_LIST` to avoid the reveal flash from #90985) stays exactly as it is:

```ts
let backTargetRoutes: NavigationPartialRoute[] | undefined;
if (focusedTargetTab.name === NAVIGATORS.WORKSPACE_NAVIGATOR) {
    // ... existing fresh WORKSPACES_LIST seeding, unchanged ...
    backTargetRoutes = [{name: SCREENS.WORKSPACES_LIST, ...(existingListParams ? {params: existingListParams} : {})}];
} else if (existingNestedRoutes?.length) {
    // Preserve the tab's entire existing stack (sidebar + any open screens) beneath the incoming
    // screen so back navigation returns to the screen the user was on, not the sidebar.
    // Drop a trailing route that duplicates the incoming screen (same name and reportID) so a
    // repeated pre-insert of the same destination stays idempotent.
    const lastExistingRoute = existingNestedRoutes.at(-1);
    const isTrailingDuplicateOfIncoming =
        lastExistingRoute?.name === newFirstRoute?.name &&
        (lastExistingRoute?.params as {reportID?: string} | undefined)?.reportID === (newFirstRoute?.params as {reportID?: string} | undefined)?.reportID;
    backTargetRoutes = isTrailingDuplicateOfIncoming ? existingNestedRoutes.slice(0, -1) : [...existingNestedRoutes];
} else {
    backTargetRoutes = defaultSidebarRouteName ? [{name: defaultSidebarRouteName}] : undefined;
}
if (backTargetRoutes?.length && newFirstRoute && backTargetRoutes.at(0)?.name !== newFirstRoute.name) {
    const prependedRoutes = [...backTargetRoutes, ...(newNestedRoutes ?? [])];
    mergedNestedState = {...focusedTargetTab.state, routes: prependedRoutes, index: prependedRoutes.length - 1};
}
```

With this change my repro test produces `[Inbox, Report(selfDM), Report(workspaceChat)]` — back returns to the self-DM, matching what the non-pre-insert dismiss path already does. All 8 existing `handleReplaceFullscreenUnderRHP` tests (the workspace-navigator seeding suite) still pass, and the cancel path is unaffected because `preInsertedOriginalTabRoute` already saves and restores the full original tab route.

This also fixes the same history loss for any other flow that pre-inserts a fullscreen while a report is open, not just the track-expense whisper.

### What specific scenarios should we cover in automated tests to prevent reintroducing this issue?

Unit tests in `tests/unit/Navigation/createRootStackNavigator/handleReplaceFullscreenUnderRHP.test.ts`:

1. Pre-inserting a workspace chat while another report (self-DM) is open in the Reports split keeps the previous report in the stack: `[Inbox, Report(A)]` + pre-insert `Report(B)` results in `[Inbox, Report(A), Report(B)]` with the index on `Report(B)`.
2. Re-dispatching the same pre-insert (the hook can recompute while the RHP is open) is idempotent — no duplicate `Report(B)` entries.
3. The existing `WORKSPACE_NAVIGATOR` seeding scenarios (#90985, #93003) are unchanged.
4. Cancelling the confirmation restores the original tab route (self-DM back on top).

### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)

- Gate the report pre-insert in `getSubmitExpensePreMountDestinationRoute` when a different report is already topmost, falling back to the plain `dismissModalWithReport` path (which pushes and preserves history). This fixes the bug but disables the flash-free reveal optimization for exactly the flow it was built for, and leaves the underlying history loss in the handler for other callers.
- Route same-tab report pre-inserts through the handler's non-tab push branch instead of the tab rebuild. This preserves history too, but bypasses the remount machinery (`markFocusedTabRouteForRemount`) that prevents the push-transition flash during the reveal, so the rebuild-with-full-history above is the safer shape.

## Proposal

### Please re-state the problem that we are trying to solve in this issue.

On web, opening an invalid magic-link URL of the form `/v/:accountID/:validateCode` (e.g. `https://staging.new.expensify.com/v/1/1`) directly in a fresh browser tab renders the "Hmm... it's not here" not-found page. Clicking **"Go back to home page"** does nothing — no navigation, no error, the page stays put. The header back button on narrow/mobile layout is dead in exactly the same way.

### What is the root cause of that problem?

`/v/1/1` matches the `VALIDATE_LOGIN` route:

https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/ROUTES.ts#L62

With `accountID=1` / `validateCode=1`, `isValidValidateCode` fails, so [`ValidateLoginPage/index.web.tsx`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/pages/ValidateLoginPage/index.web.tsx#L174-L179) renders `ValidateCodeModal`, which shows the not-found page through `FullPageNotFoundView`.

`FullPageNotFoundView` already ships **safe defaults** for both interactive elements — the link default carries a `ROUTES.HOME` fallback, so it works even with no history:

https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/BlockingViews/FullPageNotFoundView.tsx#L79-L84

```ts
onBackButtonPress = () => Navigation.goBack(),
...
onLinkPress = () => Navigation.goBackToHome(),
```

`goBackToHome()` always passes `ROUTES.HOME`:

https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/Navigation.ts#L674-L678

```ts
function goBackToHome() {
    const isNarrowLayout = getIsNarrowLayout();
    // This sets the right split navigator.
    goBack(ROUTES.HOME);
```

**The root cause is that `ValidateCodeModal` overrides `onLinkPress` with a bare `Navigation.goBack()`**, discarding that fallback:

https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/ValidateCode/ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L44-L51

```ts
onLinkPress={() => {
    Navigation.goBack();
}}
```

Inside `goBack()`, when no route is passed **and** there is no navigation history, a guard bails out and navigates nowhere:

https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/Navigation.ts#L550-L563

```ts
if (
  !backToRoute &&
  !shouldPopToSidebar &&
  !navigationRef.current?.canGoBack()
) {
  Log.hmmm("[Navigation] Unable to go back");
  return;
}
```

On a fresh tab, `!backToRoute` is `true` (nothing was passed) and `canGoBack()` is `false` (no history), so it logs `[Navigation] Unable to go back` and returns. The button is dead because the override stripped the one thing (`ROUTES.HOME`) that made the default work.

The **header back button** (narrow layout) has the _same_ root cause: `ValidateCodeModal` never sets `onBackButtonPress`, so it inherits `FullPageNotFoundView`'s fallback-less default `onBackButtonPress = () => Navigation.goBack()` and dies identically in the same fresh-tab scenario.

So this is one root cause — _`ValidateCodeModal` presents `FullPageNotFoundView` without a guaranteed Home fallback on either control_ — surfacing as two symptoms. The reported bug is the link; the back button is the same defect one hop away.

**Scope: web-only.** `ValidateLoginPage/index.tsx` (native iOS/Android) never renders `ValidateCodeModal`, so neither the bug nor the fix touches native.

### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?

Fix the root cause on both controls, but not identically — the two controls make different promises to the user and should behave accordingly:

- **The link is labeled "Go back to home page."** That's a promise, not a suggestion — it should always land on Home, with or without history.
- **The header back arrow carries no such label.** It's a generic "go back" affordance, so it should behave like one: pop real navigation history when it exists, and only fall back to Home when there's genuinely nowhere to go back to (the original bug's fresh-tab scenario).

```diff
--- a/src/components/ValidateCode/ValidateCodeModal.tsx
+++ b/src/components/ValidateCode/ValidateCodeModal.tsx
@@ -12,12 +12,13 @@ import useTheme from '@user/useTheme';
 import useThemeStyles from '@user/useThemeStyles';

 import {signInWithValidateCode} from '@user/actions/Session';
-import Navigation from '@user/Navigation/Navigation';
+import Navigation, {navigationRef} from '@user/Navigation/Navigation';
 import {isValidValidateCode} from '@user/ValidationUtils';

 import variables from '@user/variables';

 import ONYXKEYS from '@user/ONYXKEYS';
+import ROUTES from '@user/ROUTES';

 import React, {useCallback} from 'react';
 import {View} from 'react-native';
@@ -46,9 +47,7 @@ function ValidateCodeModal({code, accountID}: ValidateCodeModalProps) {
             shouldShow={!isValidCode}
             shouldForceFullScreen={!isValidCode}
             shouldShowBackButton={shouldUseNarrowLayout}
-            onLinkPress={() => {
-                Navigation.goBack();
-            }}
+            onBackButtonPress={() => (navigationRef.current?.canGoBack() ? Navigation.goBack() : Navigation.goBack(ROUTES.HOME))}
         >
             <View
                 style={styles.deeplinkWrapperContainer}
```

Two changes, one file:

1. **Remove the `onLinkPress` override.** The link then inherits `FullPageNotFoundView`'s existing default `onLinkPress = () => Navigation.goBackToHome()`, which already carries the `ROUTES.HOME` fallback and works with zero history. The override was only shadowing a correct, already-tested default — removing it deletes a place this bug class can reappear, instead of maintaining a duplicate implementation of the same fallback.
2. **Add `onBackButtonPress={() => (navigationRef.current?.canGoBack() ? Navigation.goBack() : Navigation.goBack(ROUTES.HOME))}`.** This closes the previously-unfixed hole on the narrow-layout header back button — but rather than blindly copying the link's always-Home behavior onto a control that never promised "home," it checks `canGoBack()` first: real history pop when available, Home only as the guaranteed fallback when there's none. Never dead either way.

No new user-facing strings, types, or Onyx reads are introduced — nothing to internationalize, no type casting, no state-access changes to review.

Verified manually against:

- Fresh tab, zero history (the original repro) — link navigates to Home; header back button also navigates to Home (no history to pop, correctly falls back).
- In-app client-side navigation with real history present (e.g. opened from a report) — link still forces Home (matches its label); header back button now pops back to the actual previous screen instead of forcing Home, confirmed via a temporary console-only test hook (not part of the shipped diff) that exercised client-side navigation without a full page reload.
- Multiple invalid codes (`/v/2/2`, etc.) — the fix applies uniformly.

### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)

**1. Fix only the link** (an earlier proposal on this issue):

```diff
             onLinkPress={() => {
-                Navigation.goBack();
+                Navigation.goBack(ROUTES.HOME);
             }}
```

That proposal correctly identified the root cause and even noted in a comment that the narrow-layout header back button shares the same fallback-less default — but its diff never addressed it. With only that change applied, the link works while the back button stays broken in the identical fresh-tab scenario.

## Proposal

### Please re-state the problem that we are trying to solve in this issue.

Opening `https://staging.new.expensify.com/v/1/1` directly shows the "Not here" page, but its **Go back to home page** link does nothing. On a wide screen there is no header back button either, so the page is a hard dead end — the only way out is editing the URL.

### What is the root cause of that problem?

`1` is not a valid magic code, so `ValidateCodeModal` renders the blocking "Not here" view — and it hands that view a **fallback-less** `Navigation.goBack()`, which is a documented no-op when `/v/...` is the only route in the stack.

1. `isValidValidateCode('1')` is `false` ([ValidationUtils.ts#L373-L375](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/ValidationUtils.ts#L373-L375)), so `ValidateCodeModal` renders `FullPageNotFoundView` with `shouldShow` + `shouldForceFullScreen` ([ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L44-L52](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/ValidateCode/ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L44-L52)).
2. That same JSX **overrides** the link handler with a bare `Navigation.goBack()` ([ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L49-L51](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/ValidateCode/ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L49-L51)), discarding the component's default `Navigation.goBackToHome()` ([FullPageNotFoundView.tsx#L84](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/BlockingViews/FullPageNotFoundView.tsx#L84)).
3. On a cold load of `/v/...` the root stack has exactly **one** route: `VALIDATE_LOGIN` is in `PUBLIC_SCREENS`, so `getAdaptedState` returns the state as-is instead of prepending a full-screen route underneath ([getAdaptedStateFromPath.ts#L418-L426](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/helpers/getAdaptedStateFromPath.ts#L418-L426)). That holds signed in *or* out — `/v/` is registered in both `PublicScreens` and `AuthScreens`.
4. With no `backToRoute` and `canGoBack() === false`, `goBack()` logs `[Navigation] Unable to go back` and returns without dispatching ([Navigation.ts#L550-L563](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/Navigation.ts#L550-L563)) — the button is wired up, it just never navigates.

The structural cause: the override assumes `/v/` always has history behind it. It does not — it is a **link-entry route**. The repo already knows this. The sibling modal in the same folder carries the comment *"navigate/goBack no-op from the public `/v/` route when it's the stack root"* and resets the stack instead ([ExpiredValidateCodeModal.tsx#L47-L55](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/ValidateCode/ExpiredValidateCodeModal.tsx#L47-L55)), and `ValidateLoginPage` does the same for its 2FA hand-off ([index.web.tsx#L123-L134](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/pages/ValidateLoginPage/index.web.tsx#L123-L134)). `ValidateCodeModal` never got it — the override was carried forward verbatim from the pre-`FullPageNotFoundView` code in ``Expensify/App#52407``.

Every affected exit from this page:

- **Wide layout (the repro):** the link is the *only* exit — `shouldShowBackButton={shouldUseNarrowLayout}` hides the header back button ([ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L48](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/ValidateCode/ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L48)). Dead end.
- **Narrow layout / mWeb:** the header back button *is* shown, but `ValidateCodeModal` doesn't override `onBackButtonPress`, whose default is the *same* bare `goBack()` ([FullPageNotFoundView.tsx#L81](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/BlockingViews/FullPageNotFoundView.tsx#L81)). Also dead — a second broken path a link-only fix misses.
- **Signed-in and signed-out:** both, per step 3.
- **Platform:** web/desktop only — native `ValidateLoginPage/index.tsx` never renders `ValidateCodeModal`, which is why this is a Web-only report.

### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?

In [`ValidateCodeModal.tsx`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/components/ValidateCode/ValidateCodeModal.tsx#L44-L52), replace the fallback-less handler with one that resets to `TAB_NAVIGATOR` when there is nothing to pop, and wire it to **both** exits:

```tsx
const goHome = useCallback(() => {
    Navigation.isNavigationReady().then(() => {
        if (navigationRef.current?.canGoBack()) {
            Navigation.goBack();
            return;
        }
        navigationRef.reset({index: 0, routes: [{name: NAVIGATORS.TAB_NAVIGATOR}]});
    });
}, []);
```

then pass `onLinkPress={goHome}` and `onBackButtonPress={goHome}`.

`TAB_NAVIGATOR` is the one target correct in both stacks: `PublicScreens` registers it as `SignInPage`, `AuthScreens` as the tab navigator whose `initialRouteName` is `SCREENS.HOME` ([config.ts#L2173-L2178](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/linkingConfig/config.ts#L2173-L2178)) — so the link really does go "home" for both. Regression safety: the `canGoBack()` branch keeps today's behaviour whenever `/v/` was reached from inside the app, and nothing shared or exported changes, so other `FullPageNotFoundView` consumers are untouched.

**Why the obvious one-line fix does not work.** The tempting fix is "delete the override and let the default `Navigation.goBackToHome()` run". That is *also* a no-op. It calls `goBack(ROUTES.HOME)` → `goUp()` ([Navigation.ts#L450-L537](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/Navigation.ts#L450-L537)); the root state holds only `VALIDATE_LOGIN`, so `indexOfBackToRoute` is `-1` and `distanceToPop = 1 - (-1) - 1 = 0`. `compareParams` defaults to `true` ([#L435-L438](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/50938ee687c87107298f20d36e24a6e300f7e0d2/src/libs/Navigation/Navigation.ts#L435-L438)), so the `!compareParams` POP_TO branch is skipped, the `TAB_NAVIGATOR` branch needs `distanceToPop > 0`, and `goUp` falls through to `if (distanceToPop <= 0) return false;` — **no dispatch at all**. The stack must be *reset*, not popped.

### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)

1. **Remove the `onLinkPress` override** (the spot fix most likely to be proposed) — proven dead above, and it still leaves the narrow-layout header back button broken.
2. **`Navigation.goBack(ROUTES.HOME)`** — same `goUp()` path as (1), same `distanceToPop <= 0` return.
3. **Prepend a full-screen route for `VALIDATE_LOGIN` in `getAdaptedStateFromPath`** so there is always something to pop back to. It reverts the `PUBLIC_SCREENS` guard that exists on purpose ("TabNavigator doesn't exist — causing the RESET action to fail"), risking every `/v/`, `/unlink-login/` and SAML deep link. Too broad for one dead link.
